<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<gpx version="1.1" creator="book_route.py" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1">
<metadata><name>Elk Meadows</name><desc>or-vielbig-2e:198-1: route read from the book's text and sketch map. One trkseg per waypoint pair, in order; segment sources are in the trk desc. Geometry from OSM (ODbL, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors) and USFS EDW (public domain) where marked; 'straight' segments are off-trail connectors, not traced.</desc></metadata>
<wpt lat="45.321340" lon="-121.617170"><ele>1299.1</ele><name>Clark Creek Sno-Park</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin th:clark-creek-sno-park (on OR 35; lot unmapped); confidence: medium; pdf_page: 197; quote: From Clark Creek Sno-Park ski a trail 150 yards to the junction where the Clark Creek Trail starts. Here turn left</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.324222" lon="-121.620670"><ele>1325.7</ele><name>Old Elk Meadows Trail, east end</name><desc>source: OSM way 146985885 'Old Elk Meadows Trail' east end (the 1.2-mile built-for-skiing trail); confidence: medium; pdf_page: 197; quote: at first along a 1.2-mile built-for-skiing trail to the Clark Creek single-log bridge</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.328930" lon="-121.630932"><ele>1387.7</ele><name>Joins the summer Elk Meadows Trail (Clark Creek bridge)</name><desc>source: OSM: Old Elk Meadows Trail meets Elk Meadows Trail #645; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 197; quote: to the Clark Creek single-log bridge where it joins the summer Elk Meadows hiking trail</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.334935" lon="-121.626145"><ele>1405.3</ele><name>Newton Creek crossing</name><desc>source: OSM node 1601784626, end of Newton Creek Trail #646 on #645; DEM 4,610 ft; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 199; book_elev_ft: 4640; quote: ski to Newton Creek via the Elk Meadows Trail. Cross the creek</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.340871" lon="-121.623195"><ele>1607.3</ele><name>Elk Mountain Saddle</name><desc>source: OSM junction Elk Meadows Trail #645 x Gnarl Ridge Trail #652; DEM 5,273 ft; confidence: high; pdf_page: 199; book_elev_ft: 5260; quote: follow the unmarked summer hiking trail upward steeply as it zigzags to Elk Mountain Saddle at 5,260 feet</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.342004" lon="-121.619987"><ele>1580.9</ele><name>Elk Meadows Perimeter Trail junction (meadow's south-west edge)</name><desc>source: OSM node 1601784984, Elk Meadows Trail #645 x Elk Meadows Perimeter #645A; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 200; quote: ski northeast and down from the saddle through gently sloping forest 0.5 mile to the large, scenic meadow</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.344100" lon="-121.616800"><ele>1546.9</ele><name>Elk Meadows</name><desc>source: OSM way 393921516 'Elk Meadows' (natural=grassland), centre; map 42 labels the meadows 5100'; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 200; book_elev_ft: 5100; quote: the large, scenic meadow where there is an exceptional view of Hood. From Clark Creek Sno-Park it is 4 miles to Elk Meadows.</desc></wpt>
<trk><name>Elk Meadows</name><desc>1. Clark Creek Sno-Park -&gt; Old Elk Meadows Trail, east end: straight (low), 0.26 mi | 2. Old Elk Meadows Trail, east end -&gt; Joins the summer Elk Meadows Trail (Clark Creek bridge): osm (medium), 0.65 mi | 3. Joins the summer Elk Meadows Trail (Clark Creek bridge) -&gt; Newton Creek crossing: osm (high), 0.52 mi | 4. Newton Creek crossing -&gt; Elk Mountain Saddle: osm (high), 0.97 mi | 5. Elk Mountain Saddle -&gt; Elk Meadows Perimeter Trail junction (meadow's south-west edge): osm (high), 0.18 mi | 6. Elk Meadows Perimeter Trail junction (meadow's south-west edge) -&gt; Elk Meadows: straight (medium), 0.21 mi</desc>
